# Edit in BertCut: the button on a video's preview that hands the video to BertCut, a separate
# program the user may or may not have.
#
# Nothing here presses play, and nothing is started: the run's launcher records what it was asked
# for and refuses. A run begins with BertCut absent whatever this machine has; `pose-installed`
# says otherwise, and `locate-bertcut` answers "Where is BertCut?" as Windows' picker would.

tree .
media-fixture Media
write Tools/BertCut.exe 64
refresh
go Media
preview on

# --- a video always offers the button, found or not ---

select clip.mp4
settle 400
assert-preview media
assert-visible PreviewEdit
assert-command file.edit-in-bertcut available
shot 01-edit-button PreviewPane

# --- pressed with no BertCut anywhere: nothing starts, and the status says what is wanted ---

assert-not-launched
press PreviewEdit
assert-not-launched
assert-status choose BertCut.exe

# --- the answer is kept, and the Edit that asked runs ---

locate-bertcut Tools/BertCut.exe
assert-launches 1
assert-launch-args Tools\BertCut.exe
assert-launch-args clip.mp4"

# --- remembered: the next press asks nothing ---

press PreviewEdit
assert-launches 2
assert-launch-args Tools\BertCut.exe

# --- and it is on the Preview page, where it can be changed ---

settings preview
shot 02-settings-row
settings close

# --- the same command, from the keyboard's side ---

run file.edit-in-bertcut
assert-launches 3

# --- the user's own answer wins over an installed copy ---

pose-installed bertcut
press PreviewEdit
assert-launches 4
assert-launch-args Tools\BertCut.exe

# --- sound is not video ---

select tone.wav
settle 400
assert-preview media
assert-hidden PreviewEdit
assert-command file.edit-in-bertcut unavailable Select one video.
assert-launches 4
